dua yao wes oke bbj bin ish iso swc kon kri pcm) with per-language `basis`, `usable` (false = detector off), `gate_ok` (false for all 16: nothing rebuilt may fail a sample), `usable_reason`, leave-one-set-out numbers; sets under 100 sentences are fitted but never judged, 100-199 by the Clopper-Pearson upper bound; urh: copy on, stop-word off, padding off (3.3 % > 3 %), basis `jw_pivot + gemini_silver_check`. `--retime-all` refits pad (61 languages) and stop-word (60) with the segmental ratio (`ttr_mode seg100`) and the real documents: human-document pad FP 0.7 / 4.8 / 1.0 / 0.2 / 0 % (v2 5 / 14 / 31 / 81 / 100 %). (3) Code, flag-gated: `Anchors2` reads `usable` / `gate_ok` / `ttr_mode`; `_stuff_gate` honours `gate_ok`; patches in `patches/anchors_v3_D68_*.patch` (verified with `patch --dry-run` on the live tree `gemma_mt_run2`); restart = only `reward.anchors_calibration_path -> anchors_v3.json` plus those patches. (4) Gemini Urhobo silver set (230 pairs, generated by Gemini, not native-verified): used only as a check: the urh detectors flag 0 of 48 / 170 silver sentences (v2 too) like the held-out JW text (consistent, bound 2.2 %); 34.5 % of its word types are unseen in our SFT corpus (JW held-out 5.4 %), templated connectors khwọndeniefẹ 17.7 / 1,000 tokens (JW 0); chrF++ agreement with Gemini-Urhobo (set A 60 phrases / B-F 170 sentences kept apart, bootstrap 95 %): final_1433 14.5 [11.9, 17.6] / 24.7 [23.8, 25.7], A2W alpha 0.7 13.0 [10.6, 15.9] / 22.9 [21.9, 23.9], published <HF_ORG> 8.7 / 13.4; later RL checkpoints not on the box (no weights in `runs/final2/last`), not evaluated. (5) `scripts/refit_urh_bench.py` re-runs everything on a native-verified benchmark (FP with exact upper bounds, refit that can only loosen, dev chrF++ harness entry); 100 sentences cannot certify a rate below 3 % (0 of 100 -> <= 3.0 %). Tests: `tests/test_anchors_v3.py` (9), `tests/test_anchors_v2.py` (20); full suite 900 passed, 11 skipped.
