ry pair checked on both sides against the protected index (6 IbomMT hits dropped). NOT used: MT560 / OPUS (web-mined and religious text, no row-level provenance), Pontoon / Weblate (UI strings), sudoping01 Wolof (provenance undocumented), the Bible (cap 25 % of the reference rows would apply, none in release 1), MAFAND train (owner), and Vukuzenzele eval / test (CC-BY-4.0, SFT read train only) because the corpus is lower-cased on both sides (no upper-case letter in any row): a case-sensitive chrF++ against it would reward lower-cased output. CAVEAT: the IbomMT train pairs were in the SFT data (once); the AfriScience train pairs were not in the A0 / stage-B packs (the science SFT stage has not run), but may overlap through other sources (unmeasured: the shards hold tokens only). Coverage: 8 of the 84 RL languages (none of the weak tail languages kbp nus kea kam bam mos umb kmb ... has a non-religious human source); with 15 % of the draws on 8 languages those get ~1.9 % each. Tests `tests/test_reference_reward.py` (7).
