+**D-71 Advantage std floor + per-prompt group statistics (owner 2026-11-03, 385M run; default OFF in code (`adv_std_floor: 0`, `log_group_stats: false`), `adv_std_floor: 0.02` and `log_group_stats: true` in rl_A_b64 / rl_B1_b256 / rl_C_mixed / rl_F_final).** `grpo._denominator`: advantage = (r - mean) / max(std, adv_std_floor) instead of / (std + 1e-4), in all three advantage functions; a group with std below the floor keeps the shape of its advantages at a magnitude std / floor < 1 (jitter in the third decimal of a QE score is no longer blown up to |A| ~ 1); exactly flat groups stay 0. Floor 0.02 reward units (~0.005 QE units at the shaping slope of ~4 reward units per QE unit) because the preflight did not log within-group stds (only the pooled `reward_std` 0.55-0.77 and `flat_group_frac` median 0.016): a larger value could have shrunk every advantage. `log_group_stats` writes `<out_dir>/group_stats.jsonl` (prompt index, language, bin, domain, std, mean, hard failures, guide flag per generated group) and `group_std/p05..p75`; `scripts/group_std_percentiles.py` turns it into the percentiles to re-set the floor (about the 10th percentile) at a checkpoint boundary; it is also the input of a later prompt replay by learnability (not implemented). Tests `tests/test_adv_floor_guide.py`.
+
+**D-72 Beam-guided group member (owner 2026-11-03, 385M run; default OFF in code (`guide_fraction: 0`), `guide_fraction: 0.25`, `guide_beams: 4`, `guide_adv_share_cap: 0.25` in rl_A_b64 / rl_B1_b256 / rl_C_mixed / rl_F_final, 0 in F2).** For `guide_fraction` of the prompts of a step the beam-4 translation of the CURRENT policy (`sampling.generate_beam_completions`, HF `generate` on the trainer's policy, same prompt ids / stop ids / max_new_tokens as the sampling) replaces the last sampled member of the group (group size unchanged; `Sample.guide`): scored like any member (guards, penalties, reference term), part of the group mean / std, KL term and KL record like the greedy member (the loop has no KL exclusion for the greedy member), skipped by the sampler log-prob check and the confidence rules. Off-policy: its token log-probs are the current policy's (teacher forcing) with the ratio fixed at 1 (single update per batch), no importance weight. A guide with a hard failure is dropped from its group (`grpo.group_advantages*(drop=...)`: out of mean / std, advantage 0; dynamic sampling measures informativeness without it; a non-failed guide counts, so a group informative only because of the guide is kept). `guide_adv_share_cap`: the guides' share of the step's token-weighted |advantage| is limited to the cap (`grpo.cap_member_share`). Requires `hard_fail_mask: off`. HF beam search instead of a vLLM beam op: the engine protocol has no beam command; cost = one beam search per guided prompt on the training GPU (logged: `guide/seconds`, `guide/overhead_frac`). Logging per step and per language (`guide_by_language.json`): guide / MBR pick of the group's own samples (chrF++ agreement; not added) / greedy member / group mean rewards and how often each is the best member, win rate of the guide (decode study: MBR-16 > beam-4 mainly in weak languages, so the guide may later be switched per language). MBR-from-samples as the guide itself was not implemented (it is already a member of the group, adding it would only double-count it). Tests `tests/test_adv_floor_guide.py`.
